  "digests": {
    "28": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tragedy in Japan",
          "heading": "Fijian forward Saimoni Vunilagi dies in Japan after suspected training heatstroke",
          "body": "The Fijian rugby community is mourning the tragic death of Saimoni Vunilagi, aged 26, who passed away in Japan on Friday. His club, second-division side Kyuden Voltex, confirmed the former Tokyo Sungoliath back-rower was hospitalised on Monday after showing severe symptoms of heatstroke following team practice in Fukuoka, where temperatures reached 35 degrees. Despite the best efforts of medical staff, Vunilagi could not be saved. The forward, who began his professional career in 2023, had only recently joined Kyushu KV in July."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "CONTRACT IMPASSE",
          "heading": "Eddie Hearn demands Northampton Saints make Henry Pollock a seven-figure player",
          "body": "Negotiations between Northampton Saints and Henry Pollock remain at an impasse following Eddie Hearn’s demand for a £1m annual salary. Hearn, representing the 21-year-old flanker, insists the England starlet should become the Premiership’s first seven-figure player to ensure his long-term future at Franklin’s Gardens. While some analysts have labelled the valuation as \"laudable but laughable\" for a player who was sin-binned during the recent victory in Santiago, the pressure on Saints to secure their breakout talent is mounting."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Thomas Ramos confirms Toulouse departure ahead of move to Racing 92",
          "body": "Thomas Ramos is set to leave Toulouse for Racing 92, confirming a major shift in his professional career for the 2027-28 season. Addressing the move, Ramos stated: “This decision was particularly difficult to make.” The French international fullback has spent a long tenure with the club, and his exit marks the end of a significant chapter for the reigning champions. Reports indicate he will link up with his new side following his final campaign in his current colours."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Concussion litigation",
          "heading": "High Court legal action regarding rugby concussion claims remains currently unresolved",
          "body": "The ongoing High Court legal action concerning rugby concussion claims remains active, with the status of various strikeout applications currently awaiting a definitive judicial outcome. As reported previously, the litigation continues to be a focal point for the sport, yet there have been no further updates or resolutions regarding the proceedings in recent days. Stakeholders and observers remain in a holding pattern as the court continues to weigh the arguments presented by all parties involved in the landmark case."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Ion Neculai joins Northampton Saints after departing Italian club Zebre Parma",
          "body": "Italian international tight-head prop Ion Neculai has signed for Northampton Saints. The 25-year-old makes the move to the Premiership champions following a five-season stint at Zebre Parma, where he totalled 51 appearances. Neculai, who holds four senior Italy caps, featured for the Azzurri as recently as last month’s Nations Championship fixture against Australia. Saints director of rugby Phil Dowson described the forward as a \"very physical prop who enjoys the tough side of the game.\""
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching change",
          "heading": "Sione Fukofuka steps down as Scotland Women head coach citing stress",
          "body": "Sione Fukofuka has resigned as Scotland Women’s head coach, citing the \"stress and the strain\" of being separated from his family in Australia. Fukofuka, who led the side through the 2026 Six Nations, confirmed that he requested a release from his contract on compassionate grounds. Forwards coach Dave Butcher has been appointed as interim head coach as the squad prepares for the upcoming Vodafone Scotland WXV series, with squad training scheduled to begin at Oriam this Monday."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ranking boost",
          "heading": "Wales return to world top 10 despite heavy Nations Championship defeat",
          "body": "Wales have returned to the top 10 of the World Rugby rankings for the first time since July 2024. Despite a difficult recent result against South Africa, Wales climbed one spot to 10th following Australia’s narrow victory over Japan in Osaka. This shift in the global standings sees Japan drop two places, allowing Wales to edge ahead of Italy as they continue their preparations for the upcoming autumn campaign."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match report",
          "heading": "Los Pumas fall to Springboks after Benjamin Grondona scores opening try",
          "body": "Argentina produced a formidable display on Saturday, but ultimately fell 17-10 to the world champion Springboks at Vélez. Los Pumas dictated the tempo early, with Benjamin Grondona powering over in the 10th minute following a dominant opening period. Despite aggressive line speed and constant pressure at the breakdown that disrupted South African rhythm, the visitors’ bench proved decisive in the final quarter. The defeat concludes a challenging week for Felipe Contepomi’s side following disciplinary issues surrounding the squad’s recent officiating concerns."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Winning start",
          "heading": "Les Kiss guides Australia to narrow victory over Japan in Osaka",
          "body": "The Les Kiss era began with a hard-fought 35-32 victory over Japan on Saturday, as the Wallabies survived a second-half deficit and a red card. Miles Amatosero was sent off for a high tackle on Warner Dearns, forcing the visitors to play with 14 men for a 20-minute period. Despite the pressure, tries from Harry Potter, Tom Wright, Max Jorgensen, Fraser McReight and Taniela Tupou secured the win. Kiss noted, “Smooth waters at the moment. They can get rough at any time.”"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Narrow defeat",
          "heading": "Japan suffer heart-wrenching loss as Australia edge past in Osaka",
          "body": "The Brave Blossoms fell 35-32 to Australia in a dramatic Lipovitan D Challenge Cup clash on Saturday. Despite a strong performance that capitalised on an early red card for Australian lock Miles Amatosero, Japan could not overcome the visitors’ physicality in the sweltering Osaka heat. Ryunosuke Ito, Faulua Makisi, Kazuma Ueda, and captain Warner Dearns crossed for Japan, but the home side ultimately came up just short in the dying minutes of a competitive, high-tempo international fixture."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection scrutiny",
          "heading": "New Zealand media criticise All Blacks performance following win over Stormers",
          "body": "The All Blacks secured a victory against the Stormers in their opening tour match, but the performance drew criticism from New Zealand media. Commentators noted deficiencies in the scrum, handling of high balls and defensive work at the driving maul. Head coach Dave Rennie acknowledged the team is currently building depth and stated that the squad will see significant changes for the upcoming match against the Sharks on Tuesday."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-08-09",
      "edition": "Sunday 9 August",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Ranking alert",
          "heading": "Springboks risk losing world No. 1 spot against feisty Argentina side",
          "body": "South Africa enters today’s fixture in Buenos Aires aware that their position at the top of the World Rugby rankings is under threat. While a win offers no additional rating points due to the current differential, defeat could see the Springboks overtaken by the All Blacks. Rassie Erasmus’ men must be wary of an Argentina side that has shown significant ambition, with Los Pumas looking to capitalise on the visitors’ need to maintain defensive intensity ahead of the upcoming series against New Zealand."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    }
  }
